            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0058" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.92/493</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornbeck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">of a
                        Conversation With the British Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Butler</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-01-30">January 30, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In regard to the fact that Japan is undertaking to mediate between the French
                    (Indochina) and Thailand: Mr. Butler expressed the opinion that the British and
                    the American Governments ought to signify to the Japanese Government that we
                    continue to have an interest in the matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">tanley</hi>] K. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ornbeck</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
